 Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 8 x 6 cm purple bruise, tender; left hip and both thighs intact.\n- Pain 0/10; none.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 8 x 6 cm purple bruise, tender; left hip and both thighs intact. Braden 21.\n- Fall risk: High; fall precautions in place.\n- Lines: none.\n\n**Education**\n- Oriented to room, call light, plan of care, and fall precautions.\n\n**Plan**"},{"id":"note_hospitalist_history_and_physical_2026_10_20_07_15","type":"hp","title":"Hospitalist History and Physical","author":"S. Patel, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:15","category":"H&P","summary":"Admission H&P for hypokalemia after infectious diarrhea.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Diarrhea, fever and muscle cramps\n\n**History of present illness**\n74-year-old female with type 2 diabetes and 3 days of watery diarrhea, fever and vomiting after a restaurant meal, with weak, crampy legs. Potassium 3.3 mmol/L (low), glucose high, stool culture pending. Admitted for oral potassium, an intramuscular antibiotic and sliding-scale insulin. She bruised her right hip in a fall in the bathroom last night.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for diarrhea, nausea, vomiting, fever, leg cramps and a bruised right hip. Negative for chest pain, blood in stool and shortness of breath.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 100.7 F, HR 96, BP 117/70, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 0/10 | Wt 63 kg, BMI 24.6\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 8 x 6 cm purple bruise, tender; left hip and both thighs intact.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: \n\n**Assessment and plan**\n74-year-old female with no significant history admitted with hypokalemia after infectious diarrhea.\n\n**Hypokalemia after infectious diarrhea**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"74-year-old female presenting with diarrhea, fever and muscle cramps; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Diarrhea, fever and muscle cramps\n\n**HPI**\n74-year-old female with type 2 diabetes and 3 days of watery diarrhea, fever and vomiting after a restaurant meal, with weak, crampy legs. Potassium 3.3 mmol/L (low), glucose high, stool culture pending. Admitted for oral potassium, an intramuscular antibiotic and sliding-scale insulin. She bruised her right hip in a fall in the bathroom last night.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 100.8 F, HR 97, BP 116/69, RR 16, SpO2 97% on room air, pain 0/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 8 x 6 cm purple bruise, tender; left hip and both thighs intact.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: Potassium 3.3 (L)\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 potassium chloride (K-DUR) extended-release 20 mEq Oral\n- 0445 insulin lispro (HUMALOG) Per high-dose sliding scale Subcutaneous\n- 0445 ceftriaxone (ROCEPHIN) 1.5 g Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Hypokalemia after infectious diarrhea. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuilder":{"builderVersion":2,"inputs":{"name":"Beverly Hayes","age":74,"sex":"Female","mrn":"SIM-30419","unit":"Medical-Surgical 2 East","room":"220-2","heightCm":160,"weightKg":63,"primary":"lpn_potassium","hospitalDay":1,"simDate":"2026-10-20","startTime":"08:45","hx":[],"surg":[],"surgText":"","allergies":[],"codeStatus":"Full Code","social":{"tobacco":"Never","alcohol":"None","drugs":"None","living":"Lives with spouse/partner","function":"Independent","other":""},"studentLevel":"First-semester LPN","complexity":"simple","facultyNotes":"","id":"lpn_potassium","desc":"PO potassium chloride ER 20 mEq (very large tablet), SubQ insulin lispro (high scale, glucose 316 = 16 units), IM ceftriaxone 1.5 g = 3 mL (bruised right hip: choose another site)"}}}}